{"type":"standard","title":"Justin J. Pearson","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Justin J. Pearson</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q116739449","titles":{"canonical":"Justin_J._Pearson","normalized":"Justin J. Pearson","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Justin J. Pearson</span></span>"},"pageid":72987367,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Justin_J_Pearson_August_2023.jpg/330px-Justin_J_Pearson_August_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":440},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/23/Justin_J_Pearson_August_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":1884,"height":2512},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1377061742","tid":"729505d8-baa3-11f1-ac73-5a76a48f6430","timestamp":"2026-09-27T18:44:19Z","description":"American politician (born 1995)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_J._Pearson","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_J._Pearson?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_J._Pearson?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Justin_J._Pearson"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_J._Pearson","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Justin_J._Pearson","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_J._Pearson?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Justin_J._Pearson"}},"extract":"Justin Jamal Pearson is an American activist and politician. He is a member of the Tennessee House of Representatives representing the 86th district, covering parts of the city of Memphis. He was elected in a January 2023 special election to succeed Barbara Cooper, who was posthumously re-elected in the November 2022 Tennessee House of Representatives election after dying in October 2022. When he was sworn into office at the age of 28, Pearson became the third youngest lawmaker serving in the Tennessee House of Representatives.","extract_html":"<p><b>Justin Jamal Pearson</b> is an American activist and politician. He is a member of the Tennessee House of Representatives representing the 86th district, covering parts of the city of Memphis. He was elected in a January 2023 special election to succeed Barbara Cooper, who was posthumously re-elected in the November 2022 Tennessee House of Representatives election after dying in October 2022. When he was sworn into office at the age of 28, Pearson became the third youngest lawmaker serving in the Tennessee House of Representatives.</p>"}